<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Hermes Messenger</title>
    <script src="/socket.io/socket.io.js"></script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/chatstyles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="chat-container">
        <div class="contacts-list">
            <h2>Contacts</h2>
            <ul class="chat-contacts">
                <li class="active">Socrates</li>
                <li>Plato</li>
                <li>Aristotle</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="chat-window">
            <div class="chat-header">
                <h2>Socrates</h2>
                <div class="btn-close">X</div>
            </div>
            <div class="chat-messages">
                <div class="message received">
                    <span class="sender">Socrates:</span>
                    <p>What is the nature of knowledge, my friend?</p>
                </div>
                <div class="message sent">
                    <span class="sender">You:</span>
                    <p>An intriguing question, Socrates. Perhaps knowledge is the understanding of one's own ignorance?</p>
                </div>
                <div class="message received">
                    <span class="sender">Socrates:</span>
                    <p>Ah, a wise observation. Let us delve deeper into this topic.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="message sent">
                    <span class="sender">You:</span>
                    <p>Indeed. How do we distinguish between true knowledge and mere opinion?</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="chat-input">
                <form id="form-chat">
                    <input type="text" id="input-chat" placeholder="Type your message...">
                    <button>Send</button>
                </form>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
  <script>
    

   </script>
</body>
</html>